---
import ResourceArticle from "@/layouts/ResourceArticle.astro";
import { resources } from "@/lib/resources";
---
<ResourceArticle page={resources.calcbar}>
  <p>If you use CalcBar 1.6 for quick calculations while you work, EvaBar will feel familiar. Both apps let you open a calculator with a shortcut, type a full expression, and pin the panel above other windows. If you’re planning a macOS upgrade, check which builds your Mac can run.</p>

  <h2>Key differences</h2>
  <table class="resource-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Topic</th><th scope="col">CalcBar 1.6</th><th scope="col">EvaBar</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Price and distribution</th><td>Previously sold on the Mac App Store</td><td>Free downloads through GitHub Releases, with source under the MIT license</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Minimum macOS version</th><td>macOS 11.1</td><td>macOS 13</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Apple silicon</th><td>Intel build via Rosetta on supported macOS versions through macOS 27</td><td>Native Apple silicon download (<code>arm64</code>)</td></tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Large-number precision</th>
        <td>Outputs double-precision results, which can round large integers.</td>
        <td>Preserves large integer digits in decimal arithmetic. <code>9007199254740992 + 1</code> gives <strong>9,007,199,254,740,993</strong> with comma grouping.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Long results</th>
        <td>The result field clips text that exceeds its width.</td>
        <td>The panel expands and wraps the result onto as many lines as needed.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Interface languages</th>
        <td>English in the archived listing.</td>
        <td>Follows the system language by default. Choose from <a href={`${resources.features.path}#startup-and-language`}>10 interface languages</a> in Preferences.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Appearance</th>
        <td>Original panel appearance.</td>
        <td>Switch between <a href={`${resources.features.path}#appearance`}>native Liquid Glass and classic frosted glass</a> on macOS 26 and later. Earlier supported versions use classic frosted glass.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="resource-source">Compatibility and result behavior are based on the inspected CalcBar 1.6 bundle (build 2.6). Price and language information comes from the <a href="https://calcbar-k25x9c.appstor.io/">archived CalcBar listing</a>.</p>

  <h2>Rosetta and macOS 28 on Apple silicon</h2>
  <p>On an Apple silicon Mac, CalcBar 1.6 relies on Rosetta to run its Intel build. Apple says that starting with macOS 28, Rosetta will be available only for certain older games. Under that policy, CalcBar 1.6 is expected to stop running on Apple silicon.</p>
  <p class="resource-source"><a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/102527">Apple’s guidance on Rosetta and Intel-based apps</a>.</p>

  <h2>Set up EvaBar on your Mac</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open <strong>Apple menu → About This Mac</strong> to confirm you’re running macOS 13 or later and check whether your Mac has Apple silicon or an Intel processor.</li>
    <li><a href="/#download">Download the EvaBar build</a> that matches your processor, unzip it, and move the app to Applications.</li>
  </ol>
</ResourceArticle>
